WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.770
Listen, where we are with science and
technology is a completely contingent

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.000
matter. I mean, there's nothing inevitable
about it. The Industrial Revolution: why

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.630
would it happen - who would have predicted
it would happen in some grisly, rainy

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:19.380
bits of North England in the 18th
century? Well, there was coal elsewhere.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:28.019
And it could have happened anywhere. It
happened there. That's one of those frail

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:34.800
constructs that...So the other thing—just
to come back to my story about people

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:42.649
staying standing in line for an iPhone 4—
is that I was quite interested in

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:46.770
technologies that we all take for
granted, then become very grubby, you know.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.739
So, it is an absolute miracle to fly from
San Diego to San Francisco in an hour

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:59.940
and a half. But it's just such a drag.
Luggage carousel, the security. Oh yes, you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.030
can see the clouds in the Ventana
wilderness. But you know, that's just the

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:11.760
way in which an iPhone—smartphone— ends
up in your sock drawer or in the

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.340
hands of your grandchildren discarded. So
in this world I wanted the grubby

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:24.570
reality with the future poured
into it. So you could have 400 mile-an-

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:34.229
hour trains on, you know, levitated by
magnetic force, zipping you from San

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:40.200
Francisco to  LA.  But it'd be
crowded and dirty and noisy, and the

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.439
windows will be filthy, and it will just
be another bore of the, you know, the necessary

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.259
things of life. And you can't check in
your luggage, you have to heave it up

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:58.170
under the rug luggage rack yourself. And
it's that rub off of when the

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:04.020
shiny future arrives, it rapidly absorbs
itself into our endlessly untidy bedroom,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:10.720
as it were, our teenage bedroom of social
reality. That's what fascinates me.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:18.269
When messy humans get their shiny new
toys, the shine goes off very quickly.

